Register configuration (applied after SW_RESET + BOOT, in this order; FIFO_CTRL4 last starts batching)
  CTRL3_C    0x12 = 0x44  BDU | IF_INC                         DS Tab 56/57, ST reg.h:417
  CTRL9_XL   0x18 = 0xE2  DEN defaults | I3C_disable           DS Tab 73/74 (note 1 recommends it)
  FIFO_CTRL1 0x07 = 0x00  WTM[7:0] (256)                       DS Tab 32/33
  FIFO_CTRL2 0x08 = 0x01  WTM8                                 DS Tab 34/35
  FIFO_CTRL3 0x09 = 0x77  BDR_GY = BDR_XL = 833 Hz              DS Tab 36/37, ST reg.h:3694/3714
  CTRL1_XL   0x10 = 0x7C  ODR 833 Hz, FS 11 = +-8 g             DS Tab 49-52, ST reg.h:2917-2936
  CTRL2_G    0x11 = 0x7C  ODR 833 Hz, FS 110 = +-2000 dps       DS Tab 53-55, ST reg.h:2949-2969
  CTRL10_C   0x19 = 0x20  TIMESTAMP_EN                         DS Tab 75/76, Linux timer_en BIT(5)
  FIFO_CTRL4 0x0A = 0x66  DEC_TS=1, ODR_T=12.5 Hz, continuous    DS Tab 38/39, ST reg.h:3731/3743/3754
Reset: FIFO_CTRL4=0 -> CTRL3_C=0x05 -> 50 ms -> poll SW_RESET clear -> CTRL3_C=0x84 -> 50 ms -> poll BOOT clear
-> verify defaults (CTRL3_C 0x04, CTRL9_XL 0xE0, others 0) -> read INTERNAL_FREQ_FINE (Linux reset_device).

Facts confirmed (DS12814 Rev 4 is the LSM6DSOX datasheet; the plan's "DS13345" is a wrong document number)
- WHO_AM_I 0x0F = 0x6C; addr 0x6A/0x6B; sensitivities DS Table 2 = ST .c (0.061/0.122/0.244/0.488 mg/LSB;
  4.375/8.75/17.5/35/70 mdps/LSB); FS/ODR/BDR codes = ST enums (checked by test_regs against the vendored header).
- Tag byte: TAG_SENSOR[7:3], TAG_CNT[2:1], TAG_PARITY[0]; tags 1 gyro, 2 accel, 3 temp, 4 timestamp, 5 cfg.
- FIFO_STATUS2: WTM_IA b7, OVR_IA b6, FULL_IA b5, COUNTER_BDR_IA b4, OVR_LATCHED b3 (clears on read), DIFF[9:8].
- TIMESTAMP0..3 LE, 25 us/LSB; INTERNAL_FREQ_FINE int8, 0.15 %/LSB (DS Tab 174).
[AN] = not confirmed without AN5272 (taken from ST driver / Linux / DS hints; checked by ec-imu-probe on H):
- trim formula t = 25 us / (1 + 0.0015 * FREQ_FINE) (AN5192 for LSM6DSO quoted in Linux st_lsm6dsx.h:203-211);
- burst read wraps 0x7E -> 0x78 (Linux reads 4 words per transaction from 0x78);
- timestamp word first in a slot and shares TAG_CNT with its data (driver pairs by TAG_CNT, order-independent;
  ts-first pairing available); timestamp word = 32-bit LE in data bytes 0..3 (Linux);
- temperature word = int16 in data bytes 0..1; FIFO capacity 512 words; TAG_PARITY definition (unused).

Clock mapping
- Brackets: t0, TIMESTAMP0..3 read (4 B), t1; second read immediately after for the torn-read check (B-A must
  fit the elapsed time). Every poll during the first 2 s, then every bracket_period_ms.
- ChipClockMapper: slope = Huber-IRLS weighted LS on midpoints (w = 1/(width^2/12 + tick^2/12)), clamp
  nominal*(1+-3 %); offset (lower_envelope) = midpoint of [max(before - b x), min(after - b x)] over inliers;
  outlier gate 1 ms (5 consecutive restart the window). Window 300 brackets.
- Results (virtual clock, 400 kHz bus, 40 us + exp(15 us) latency, 0.5 % spikes up to 1.5 ms):
  60 s run: map error max 23.2 us, mean 18.5 us (mostly the constant latch-position bias); residual p99 33 us.
  +-2 % drift: max 27.7 / 21.6 us; slope error 0.05-0.13 ppm (synthetic mapper test: worst live error 28 us).
  100 kHz bus: constant bias 52 us, spread 7 us (bias is absorbed by the camera-IMU time offset).

Contract notes (additive with defaults; worklog-note class per STATUS.md)
- ImuConfig += timestamp_decimation=1, temperature_batch_hz=12.5, fifo_burst_words=32, pair_by_tag_counter=true
  (no yaml keys yet; T3's loader/writer can add them).
- ImuStats += freq_fine, fifo_words, fifo_full_flags, partial_slots, slots_without_timestamp,
  torn_timestamp_reads, temperature_words.
- ChipClockConfig += outlier_gate_ns=1000000.
- clock.hpp: doc comment of ClockFitMethod::kLowerEnvelope corrected (comment only; "under the before points"
  was the physically wrong side).
- No frozen declaration changed. No CMake edits.
- For T3: its poll budget check assumes 2 words per ODR; with timestamp batching it is 3 words per ODR.
- For T3/T6: yaml imu.noise.accel_noise_density 70 ug/rtHz is the +-2 g value; DS Table 2 gives 80 at +-8 g.
- For T3/T5: the poll thread inherits affinity/priority of the thread that calls start(); call it from the
  pinned IMU capture thread. ImuSample.chip_ticks + read_brackets() allow an offline refit (chip.csv).

